{
 "summary": "Adds CreateMultisigDescriptor() to script/descriptor to assemble and validate ranged, multipath multisig descriptors with checksums from a list of cosigner xpubs. The function constructs P2WSH (wsh(sortedmulti(...))) and P2TR (tr(musig(...), sortedmulti_a(...))) descriptors. It enforces setup constraints including bare account xpubs with origin info, duplicate key rejection, threshold bounds, and exclusion of private keys.",
 "problem": "Multisig setup flows have had to assemble descriptor strings manually, risking errors from unvalidated string interpolation, duplicate cosigners, invalid thresholds, or improper derivation paths.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description notes multisig setup flows need to assemble descriptors without hand-crafting strings: 'today means bash interpolation with no validation of key forms, duplicates, or threshold'",
  "Author references the multisig wizard backend tracking issue #35645 and GUI/contrib PR #36325"
 ],
